WEBVTT

1
00:00:04.300 --> 00:00:07.650 line:-2
<v Narrator>Narrator: The decisive vote of the 36th state against Prohibition

2
00:00:07.650 --> 00:00:10.750 line:-2
<v Narrator>is happy news for the grain raisers of the United States

3
00:00:10.750 --> 00:00:12.700 line:-2
<v Narrator>and for many others throughout the land.

4
00:00:13.200 --> 00:00:17.800 line:-2
<v Narrator>With an eye on December 5th, work is being rushed in distilleries and bottling works.

5
00:00:18.100 --> 00:00:20.400 line:-2
<v Narrator>There’ll be no more scenes such as this,

6
00:00:20.400 --> 00:00:23.600 line:-2
<v Narrator>barrel after barrel of prize whiskies destroyed by government agents.

7
00:00:23.700 --> 00:00:26.200 line:-2
<v Narrator>It’s gonna be a cold winter for the barrel busters!

8
00:00:26.500 --> 00:00:29.950 line:-2
<v Al Smith>Al Smith: Of course I am delighted, but not surprised

9
00:00:29.950 --> 00:00:33.500 line:-2
<v Al Smith>by the final repeal of the 18th Amendment.

10
00:00:34.000 --> 00:00:37.200 line:-2
<v Al Smith>I felt all along that when this matter was properly submitted

11
00:00:37.200 --> 00:00:39.000 line:-2
<v Al Smith>to the rank and file of our people,

12
00:00:39.000 --> 00:00:43.300 line:-2
<v Al Smith>they would readily see that it had no place in our Constitution.
